	Port support (not a DarkPlaces source file): the libm functions DarkPlaces calls, computed in pure Luau with
	the same operations as GNU libc 2.43 on x86-64 (the version the GitHub runner that writes our reference
	vectors prints), so that every result has the same bits as the C build on Linux no matter which C library
	the Luau host has (Luau's math.sin etc. call the host libm; HANDOFF G-058).

	Ported from GNU libc 2.43, sysdeps/ieee754/dbl-64/ (read from the glibc git mirror: the glibc-2.39 tag and
	master of 2026-01-20, i.e. 2.43; for every file used here the history between them is copyright years
	only, except e_pow.c / e_log.c, taken from master), files and functions named at each "port: glibc-2.43"
	comment:
